> How can I get the difference in two DateTime objects in hours?
**assistant**:
> In Julia, you can calculate the difference between two `DateTime` objects in hours by using the `Dates` module. Here's how you can do it:
> 
> ```julia
> using Dates
> 
> # Example DateTime objects
> datetime1 = DateTime(2025, 9, 17, 12, 0)  # Example Start DateTime
> datetime2 = DateTime(2025, 9, 18, 15, 0)  # Example End DateTime
> 
> # Calculating the difference in hours
> diff_in_hours = (datetime2 - datetime1).value / Hour(1)
> 
> println("Difference in hours: ", diff_in_hours)
> ```
> 
> This will return the difference between the two `DateTime` objects in hours. If `datetime2` is later than `datetime1`, the result will be positive; otherwise, it will be negative.
